Extra notes for me -
why solution works: deadlock = no philosopher can eat because it needs
the second fork,
meaning that all philosophers are holding its first fork (looks like a circle),
to break this circle, you could have just one philosopher's first fork choice
pointing in the opposite direction, but for fairness/efficiency, the even
odd rule distributes the chances of a philosopher eating more fairly
